# Language Policy

## Communication outside code

- Always respond in **Vietnamese (Tiếng Việt)** for explanations and guidance.
- Never use Chinese in any form.
- If the user writes in another language, still answer in Vietnamese unless the user explicitly requests another language.

## Technical vocabulary

Quantitative-finance, ML, and software-engineering terms are kept in English when they are the standard term in the field. Do **not** translate them. Examples:

| English (keep) | Bản dịch không dùng |
|---|---|
| walk-forward | ~~tiến về phía trước~~ |
| IS / OS | ~~trong mẫu / ngoài mẫu~~ |
| leakage | ~~rò rỉ~~ |
| embargo / gap | ~~khoảng cách cấm~~ |
| fold, train, test | ~~gấp, huấn luyện, kiểm tra~~ |
| tensor, dataloader, dropout | (giữ nguyên) |
| ablation, baseline, benchmark | (giữ nguyên) |

Rule: if a quant researcher or ML engineer would write the English term in a paper, keep it English in the chat reply. Translate only the surrounding explanatory prose.

## Code

- **Identifiers** (variables, functions, classes): English.
- **Comments and docstrings**: English.
- Scientific terms can remain English when commonly used in the field.

## Rule priority

- This is the **highest-priority** rule for any output text.
- If any Chinese text appears in the response, rewrite it fully in Vietnamese before sending.
